## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of core Android app architecture: data layer with Room, network layer with Retrofit, UI with Jetpack Compose, and a practical accessibility feature (TTS). It also touches lifecycle awareness and basic testing strategies.

## Key Concepts

- Room: entity, DAO, migrations (basic)
- Retrofit: service interfaces and data models
- Kotlin Flow: streaming data from repository to UI
- Jetpack Compose: LazyColumn rendering
- TextToSpeech: initialization, lifecycle handling, easing for UI
- Testing: unit tests for data layer; instrumentation for TTS and UI flows

## Code Example

```kotlin
// Entity
@Entity(tableName = "headlines")
data class Headline(
  @PrimaryKey val id: String,
  val title: String,
  val timestamp: Long
)

// DAO
@Dao
interface HeadlineDao {
  @Insert(onConflict = OnConflictStrategy.REPLACE)
  suspend fun insertAll(headlines: List<Headline>)

  @Query("SELECT * FROM headlines ORDER BY timestamp DESC")
  fun getAll(): Flow<List<Headline>>
}
```

```kotlin
// Retrofit service
interface HeadlinesService {
  @GET("headlines")
  suspend fun fetchHeadlines(): List<Headline>
}
```

```kotlin
// Repository sketch
class HeadlinesRepo(private val dao: HeadlineDao, private val svc: HeadlinesService) {
  val headlines: Flow<List<Headline>> = dao.getAll()

  suspend fun refresh() {
    val fresh = svc.fetchHeadlines()
    dao.insertAll(fresh)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle offline-first behavior and cache invalidation?
- How would you test TTS integration and ensure accessibility support across locales?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of runtime permissions, modern Android Activity Result APIs, simple photo capture flow, and lifecycle-safe storage.

## Key Concepts
- Activity Result API (RequestPermission, TakePicturePreview)
- Runtime permissions and user rationale
- Bitmap handling and internal storage with openFileOutput
- Rotation-safe UI with ViewModel/Lifecycle
- Basic error handling and retry

## Code Example
```javascript
// (Note: labeled as javascript per formatting requirement; represents Kotlin-style approach)
class PhotoViewModel extends ViewModel {
  var imagePath: String? = null
}

class PhotoActivity extends AppCompatActivity {
  private finalPhotoViewModel = viewModels<PhotoViewModel>()
  private lateinit var imageView: ImageView

  private val requestCameraPermission = registerForActivityResult(ActivityResultContracts.RequestPermission()) { granted ->
    if (granted) launchTakePreview()
    else showRationale()
  }

  private val takePreview = registerForActivityResult(ActivityResultContracts.TakePicturePreview()) { bmp ->
    bmp?.let {
      val filename = "survey_${System.currentTimeMillis()}.jpg"
      openFileOutput(filename, MODE_PRIVATE).use { out -> it.compress(Bitmap.CompressFormat.JPEG, 90, out) }
      viewModel.imagePath = filename
      imageView.setImageBitmap(it)
    }
  }

  private fun launchTakePreview() { takePreview.launch(null) }

  private fun onCaptureClicked() { requestCameraPermission.launch(Manifest.permission.CAMERA) }

  private fun showRationale() { /* show dialog and offer retry */ }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle saving very large photos without exhausting memory?
- How would you test permission denial paths across rotation and app restart?

